{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 39, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a thought-provoking and engaging film that delves into the true story of the founding of facebook. directed by david finchercer, the movie masterfully weaves together the complex and often tumultuous relationship between mark zuckerberg and his college roommates, edward and cambridge fellow, wilmot \"bill\" goss.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg's (jacob anderson) awkward introduction to harvard university, where he quickly makes a name for himself as a brilliant but socially inept student. mark's life takes a dramatic turn when he creates a website called \"facemash,\" which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. although facemash is initially a huge success, it also gets mark into trouble with the university administration.\n\nbefore long, mark is approached by edward and cambridge fellow, wilmot \"bill\" goss (andy garcia) and divya Narendra (drew todd), who suggest that they should create a social networking site exclusively for harvard students. mark is hesitant at first, but eventually agrees to partner with his new friends.\n\nas the movie progresses, we see the early days of facebook, which quickly becomes a sensation among harvard students. however, the site's popularity soon attracts the attention of the university's president, leno levitte (wesley snipes), who demands that mark shut down the site.\n\nmeanwhile, mark's relationships with his roommates begin to fray as they disagree on the direction of facebook. edward, who is increasingly frustrated with mark's dominance in the company, decides to leave and join palantir, a data analysis firm co-founded by peter thiel (christian baker).\n\nthe film's portrayal of mark's emotional struggle is both captivating and heartbreaking. as the pressure to keep facebook growing mounts, mark's relationships with his friends and family begin to suffer. his romantic relationship with facebook's first female employee, christy lee (megan freeman), also comes to an end due to his increasing focus on the company.\n\nthe film's climax is a tense and dramatic depiction of the lawsuit filed by the winklevoss twins, cambridge roommates and facebook investors, edward and armistead winklevoss (armie hammer). mark's response to the lawsuit is both defensive and revealing, exposing the tumultuous relationship he had with his roommates.\n\nthe social network is a gripping and thought-provoking film that raises important questions about the impact of technology on our society. the film's exploration of the darker side of ambition and the consequences of success is both timely and timeless.\n\noverall, the social network is a must-see film for anyone interested in the story behind facebook's creation. the film's performances are outstanding, the direction is masterful, and the script is witty and engaging.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.20552276074886322}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.00030310326837934554}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.04680052399635315}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0009606037638150156}, {"token": " thought", "logprob": -1.7862296104431152}, {"token": "-pro", "logprob": -4.589452510117553e-05}, {"token": "v", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oking", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.5664827823638916}, {"token": " engaging", "logprob": -0.5872182250022888}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.034964803606271744}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.008133976720273495}, {"token": " del", "logprob": -0.1450195163488388}, {"token": "ves", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " into", "logprob": -0.0008007657015696168}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " true", "logprob": -5.241487503051758}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -0.0001936963381012